Let a REGISTER replace the earlier bindings of the same UE (TS 24.229 5.4.1.2.1).

ims_usrloc_scscf matches a binding by its Contact URI only (contact_match()
and friends); +sip.instance and reg-id are stored with the binding's params
but nothing reads them. A UE that registers again from a new IP address or
port therefore gets a second binding, and the old one stays until it
expires: lookup() forks terminating requests to it, the 200 OK lists it,
and the P-CSCF keeps its contact and IPsec tunnel, since only a terminated
reg-event contact removes those.

New modparam replace_contacts, default 0. With it set, once the Contacts of
a REGISTER are inserted or updated, every other valid binding of the IMPU
that one of them replaces is de-registered:

- A Contact with a reg-id (multiple registrations, RFC 5626) replaces the
  registration flow with the same +sip.instance (URN compared without its
  angle brackets) and reg-id - step 3.
- A Contact without one replaces every earlier registration of the private
  user identity with another contact address - step 2 - whatever its
  +sip.instance, or none: a UE that sends no instance, or the same SIM in a
  new handset, is replaced too. usrloc keeps no IMPI per binding, but an
  IMPU record belongs to the one IMPI whose subscription it holds, so that
  is every other binding of the IMPU.
- An emergency (sos) Contact only replaces an emergency binding and a normal
  one only a normal one (5.4.1.2.1D NOTE 2). A Contact being removed
  (expires 0) replaces nothing, and neither is a binding the REGISTER itself
  names, so several Contacts registered together stay.

The replaced binding is de-registered on the spot, as reg_rpc_dereg_impu()
does: CONTACT_DELETED, so VALID_CONTACT() is false for it at once and the
usrloc timer only unlinks it, silently, and releases its dialogs when it
deletes it. The NOTIFY goes out now rather than on the next timer run, to
the subscribers of every IMPU of the implicit set: update_contacts_helper()
runs once per IMPU and the binding is shared, so the bindings a REGISTER
replaced are remembered for the later runs (per process, by message id and
pid). It carries the binding as an explicit de-registration contact,
terminated with event "unregistered": 5.4.2.1.2 allows only "unregistered",
"deactivated" or "rejected" for "each replaced or removed binding", and a
P-CSCF acts only on those under an active registration (5.2.5.2). The event
type is IMS_REGISTRAR_CONTACT_UNREGISTERED_IMPLICIT: _UNREGISTERED and
_EXPIRED make create_notifications() send Subscription-State: terminated,
which would end the P-CSCF's subscription while the IMPU is still registered
over the new contact.

process_xml_for_explit_dereg_contact() renders every explicit
de-registration contact with event "unregistered" instead of "expired": the
other two producers, the de-REGISTER in save.c and reg_rpc_dereg_impu()
(patch 0006), remove a binding too, and "unregistered" is what RFC 3680 and
5.4.2.1.2 / 5.4.1.5 call that.

